{
 "id": "elbow-gearbox-forearm-mjf",
 "brief": "elbow-gearbox.stl (attached, mm, placed where it sits) is the cycloidal gearbox at my robot arm's\nelbow: housing, output flange and centre spigot, axis along Y through the origin. I need the\nforearm's root, MJF PA11, bolted flat onto the flange's +Y face with M3 socket-head screws into\nthe six tapped holes on its 30 mm circle (take the positions off the STL), through a 5 mm thick\nclamping face with 3.4 mm holes; each head bears on that face and needs an 8 mm column clear along\n+Y above it for the hex key. The spigot locates in a hole in the part; nothing may enter the\ngearbox. The forearm reaches along +X to the wrist servo's mounting face, the plane x = 110: the\nservo screws onto it with four M2.5 screws into heat-set inserts (3.5 mm holes, 5 mm deep along X,\n1.5 mm of wall, a flat 6.5 mm landing on the face) at y = 9 and 29, z = -10 and 10, and its cable\nneeds an 8 mm channel along X on (y = 19, z = 0) from x = 60 to the face. The part stays in\nx = -24 to 110, y from the flange face to 34, z = -20 to 20. Loads at the wrist face: the gearbox\nstalls at 6 N.m about Y with the wrist blocked; the wrist-roll servo stalls at 2 N.m about X; and\na 20 N side knock along Y, either way. Safety factor 2, under 35 g.",
 "attachments": [
